        <groundspeak:log id="331101998">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-07-16T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP366 – Drayton Valley

Posted: N53 12.421 W114 56.350

My GPSr: N53 12.42[b]2[/b] W114 56.3[b]48[/b]

My Elevation: 811 m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As I set out to find this cap from the parking spot, I donned what is a new feature of my cap finding kit, a reflective safety vest, what I call my “cloak of invisibility”. Well it turns out I didn't even need it. There were no humans anywhere near the cap location today. What there was, was a nice quad trail and a somewhat worn trail all the way to the cap site. Very nice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And the cap must have been frightened of me for some reason: it was sweating like crazy when I found it. I wiped it off best I could and took the pics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="257875390">
          <groundspeak:date>2012-08-15T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1298988">dronnord</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 366 

Drayton Valley

N 53 12.420 W 114 56.350

Elev = 818&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was a great little walk in the bush,until I spotted the fresh bear scat. That opened my eyes and as I got a little deeper into the bush and stopped to look for the cap....the mosquitoes caught up to me.

Wow,,, I could hardly breathe without swallowing them. The rain has been unreal in Drayton Valley all week.Almost every night it has dumped so after a couple of dry days I figured I could do a few caches after work. After all I was already dirty and covered in DEET.

  Working in the fields was rough and going into the bush was a trial for sure. Thank goodness the wind is available during the day to keep them at bay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don`t let this little tale stop you from getting this great cap. The views are outstanding and you can get a great view of the new highway crossing and bridge construction. Thanks OFTH for another great adventure.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
